.TH "JSONKIT\-GET" "1" "" "jsonkit 0.0.0" ""
.SH "NAME"
jsonkit\-get \- Read one value at a path.
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.nf
\fBjsonkit get\fR <path> [options]
.fi
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
A path is a dot\-separated walk from the root of the document.
.IP \(bu 2
A \fBkey\fR reads an object\(aqs member, such as \fBuser.name\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
A \fBwhole number\fR reads an array\(aqs item, such as \fBitems.0\fR.
.PP
The document is \fIJSON\fR; see the format <https://www.json.org/json\-en.html>.
.SH "ARGUMENTS"
.TP
\fIpath\fR
Dot path to read.
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-file\fR <\fIpath\fR>
The document to read. Omit it to read piped text.  (file or piped stdin, \- selects stdin; required)
.TP
\fB\-\-compact\fR
Print the JSON on one line.
.TP
\fB\-\-indent\fR <\fIspaces\fR>
Indent nested JSON by this many spaces, from 0 to 8.  (default: 2)
.PP
Use at most one of \-\-compact and \-\-indent.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.nf
\fB$ jsonkit get name \-f doc.json\fR
.fi
.PP
.nf
\fB$ jsonkit get nested.deep.value \-f doc.json\fR
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBjsonkit\fR(1)
